<title>BELGIUM: BBL sees higher 1996 insurance profits.</title>
<headline>BBL sees higher 1996 insurance profits.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgium's Banque Bruxelles Lambert SA said on Thursday it expected net profit from its four insurance units would amount to 179 million Belgian francs, a rise of 67 percent or 72 million francs over 1995.</p>
<p>BBL's insurance activities would represent around 2.45 percent of the bank's total estimated, non-consolidated net income, the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;The bank wants to raise this contribution to five percent before the year 2000,&quot; it said.</p>
</text>
